cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this laboratory, cite this software release. Authors are preserved
  from the supplied firmware metadata.
type: software
title: 'UMSF Firmware Laboratory: A Self-Contained Colab Companion for ESP32/BLE Protocols
  and Native Logic'
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
license: MIT
abstract: An English, self-contained computational laboratory accompanying umsf-ble-firmware
  1.0.0. The notebook embeds the original source and builds its portable C/C++ libraries,
  runs all original host tests and supplied protocol vectors, and generates 30 explanatory
  figures with PNG/SVG exports. Controlled native experiments examine physiological
  feature quality, null sentinels, explicitly synthetic HR, stationary detector rules,
  gas warmup and hysteresis, tilt uncertainty, SOS debounce, link freshness, RAM-buffer
  priorities and application acknowledgements. Protocol experiments inspect CRC corruption
  and native BLE fragmentation. Includes clean and executed notebooks, a rendered
  HTML report, CSV traces, source provenance, validation evidence, citation metadata
  and MIT license. All experimental sensor inputs are synthetic. ESP32 firmware images
  are not compiled or hardware-validated in this release; hosted Google Colab frontend
  execution has not been directly tested. The notebook is verified in a fresh local
  Python/IPython process with only the notebook supplied. Thresholds are uncalibrated;
  no clinical, gas-concentration, structural-safety or causal-attribution claims are
  made.
keywords:
- ESP32
- Bluetooth Low Energy
- NimBLE
- MQTT
- firmware
- physiological monitoring
- critical infrastructure
- incident support
- dataset acquisition
